  "_TOKENS": "min_output_tokens is a floor, not a preference. Reasoning models consume the budget internally before emitting, so calling one below its floor yields empty content with HTTP 200 -- a silent no-op, not an error. Measured 2026-09-28: gpt-oss-120b emitted nothing at max_tokens=60, and score_batch's global SCORE_MAX_TOKENS=2048 starved gpt-oss-20b in prod.",
  "_CAPABILITY": "suitable_for_scoring is separate from verification. Every entry here was PROVED to respond correctly at realistic prompt size; that says nothing about whether it can reason about a job description. Selecting the pool on family diversity alone put a code model and a 2.6B model into the council and the AI Eval Gate measured tier_accuracy falling 63.2% -> 25.0%.",
  "_NVIDIA": "NVIDIA NIM entries are RETAINED BUT DISABLED. They authenticate and a single call returns 200 in ~5s, which is why they were added as an independent-quota failover. Sustained-load measurement disproved that: 2/6 back-to-back, 4/6 with a 3s gap, the rest 503. In CI the same limit surfaced as reads timing out, and the eval job was cancelled at 20 minutes having spent most of it waiting. They are kept here so the next person does not repeat the one-shot probe and reach the same conclusion.",
  "_GEMINI": "Google AI Studio, on a quota independent of both Groq and OpenRouter \u2014 the property the council was missing, and free. The key was already in SSM for pgvector embeddings; the council had simply never used it.\n\nSustained-load tested BEFORE being added, because NVIDIA passed a single probe and then 503'd under rate: gemini 24/24 back-to-back and spaced, 1.2-1.6s throughout, against NVIDIA's 2/6. A one-shot 200 is not evidence a provider can carry load, and a failover is used precisely when load is highest.",
  "_MODEL_ROT": "Free model ids are withdrawn without notice. ling-3.0-flash-fin:free was removed 2026-09-28: it is absent from OpenRouter's live /models listing (16 free models that day) and returned 404 on every CI call. Re-check this file against the live listing before trusting the entry count \u2014 a registry row is a claim about a remote catalog, and the catalog moves."
}
